---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Chart from "../components/Chart.astro";
import Fig from "../components/Fig.astro";
import {
  change, checks, compact, firstPeriod, latestPeriod, pct, periods, quarterLabel, recordSince, sources, value,
  type Measure,
} from "../lib/ledger";
import { seriesSpec } from "../lib/specs";

// Every comparison below is computed from the ledger on each build, so the words follow the data after a refresh.
const L = latestPeriod();
const F = firstPeriod();
const span = (() => { const q = (p: string) => +p.slice(2, 6) * 4 + +p.slice(-1); return (q(L) - q(F) + 1) / 4; })();
const years = span % 1 >= 0.5 ? `nearly ${Math.ceil(span)}` : `${Math.floor(span)}`;
const nSources = sources().length;
const argmax = (s: string, m: Measure, ps = periods(s, m)) => ps.reduce((a, b) => (value(s, b, m) > value(s, a, m) ? b : a));
const argmin = (s: string, m: Measure, ps = periods(s, m)) => ps.reduce((a, b) => (value(s, b, m) < value(s, a, m) ? b : a));
const since = (p: string | null, never: string) => (p ? `the fewest since ${quarterLabel(p)}` : never);

// Anchor on the lowest of the last four quarters: comparing the latest quarter to a lower one just before it says nothing.
const R = argmin("total", "approved", periods("total", "approved").slice(-4));
const apprLow = recordSince("total", "approved", R, "low");
const pendHigh = recordSince("total", "pending", L, "high");
const pendMultiple = value("total", L, "pending") / value("total", F, "pending");
const compPeak = argmax("total", "completed");
const compFirst = periods("total", "completed")[0];
const recPeak = argmax("total", "received");

const natLow = recordSince("n-400", "approved", L, "low");
const natPrevLow = argmin("n-400", "approved", periods("n-400", "approved").filter((p) => p < L));
const natYearAgo = periods("n-400", "approved").filter((p) => p < L).at(-4)!;

const asyLowest = argmin("i-589", "approved");
const asyRecPeak = argmax("i-589", "received");
const asyRecLow = recordSince("i-589", "received", L, "low");

const otherWaitYears = value("i-130-other-relative", L, "median_processing_months") / 12;
const errorCount = checks().filter((c) => c.severity === "warn").length;
const repeated = checks().filter((c) => c.check === "repeated-processing-time" && c.subject.endsWith("FY2024Q3")).length;
---
<Base
  title="USA Immigration Ledger"
  description={`USCIS approved ${compact(value("total", R, "approved"))} cases in ${quarterLabel(R)}, ${since(apprLow, "the fewest on record")}, while ${compact(value("total", L, "pending"))} wait. ${years} years of the agency's own spreadsheets, rebuilt cell by cell.`}
>
  <p class="kicker">Investigation · USCIS caseload, {quarterLabel(F)} to {quarterLabel(L)}</p>
  <h1>
    USCIS approved fewer cases {R === L ? "last quarter" : `in ${quarterLabel(R)}`} than in any quarter since {apprLow ? quarterLabel(apprLow) : quarterLabel(F)}.
    {pendHigh === null ? ` A record ${compact(value("total", L, "pending"))} are waiting.` : ` ${compact(value("total", L, "pending"))} are waiting.`}
  </h1>
  <p class="dek">
    We rebuilt {years} years of the agency's quarterly reports, cell by cell, from {nSources} government files,
    including reports USCIS has since deleted, recovered from the Internet Archive. Every number on this page links
    to the exact cell it came from.
  </p>
  <p class="byline">Data through {quarterLabel(L)} (fiscal {L.slice(0, 6)}, quarter {L.slice(-1)}) · Methodology and caveats are <a href="/methodology/">here</a></p>

  <div class="tiles">
    <div class="tile">
      <div class="label">Cases approved, {quarterLabel(R)}</div>
      <div class="value"><Fig s="total" p={R} m="approved" /></div>
      <div class="delta">{since(apprLow, `fewest since ${quarterLabel(F)}`)}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tile">
      <div class="label">Cases pending, end of {quarterLabel(L)}</div>
      <div class="value"><Fig s="total" p={L} m="pending" display={(n) => compact(n)} /></div>
      <div class="delta">{pendMultiple.toFixed(1)}× the {compact(value("total", F, "pending"))} of {quarterLabel(F)}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tile">
      <div class="label">Naturalizations approved, {quarterLabel(L)}</div>
      <div class="value"><Fig s="n-400" p={L} m="approved" /></div>
      <div class="delta">{natLow ? `fewest since ${quarterLabel(natLow)}` : `fewest of any quarter since ${quarterLabel(F)}`}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tile">
      <div class="label">Asylum applications approved, {quarterLabel(asyLowest)}</div>
      <div class="value"><Fig s="i-589" p={asyLowest} m="approved" /></div>
      <div class="delta">fewest of any quarter since {quarterLabel(F)}</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="prose">
    <p>
      U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services decides green cards, citizenship, work permits, asylum
      claims filed outside immigration court, and dozens of other benefits. Every quarter it publishes a spreadsheet
      counting, for each form, how many cases came in, how many were approved or denied, and how many are still
      waiting. It deletes old ones. We recovered every quarter back to {quarterLabel(F)}.
    </p>
    <p>
      In {quarterLabel(R)} the agency approved <Fig s="total" p={R} m="approved" /> applications and petitions,
      {" "}{since(apprLow, `the fewest of any quarter since ${quarterLabel(F)}`)}{R !== L ? <>, and <Fig s="total" p={L} m="approved" /> in {quarterLabel(L)}</> : ""}. The queue kept growing:
      {" "}<Fig s="total" p={L} m="pending" /> cases were pending at the end of the quarter,
      {" "}{pendHigh === null ? "the most in any report since our records begin" : `the most since ${quarterLabel(pendHigh)}`},
      against <Fig s="total" p={F} m="pending" /> in {quarterLabel(F)}.
    </p>
    <p>
      The slowdown is recent. Since {quarterLabel(compFirst)} USCIS also prints total completions (approvals plus
      denials and other outcomes). They peaked at <Fig s="total" p={compPeak} m="completed" /> in
      {" "}{quarterLabel(compPeak)} and were <Fig s="total" p={L} m="completed" /> in {quarterLabel(L)}, down
      {" "}{pct(-change("total", "completed", compPeak, L))}. Filings fell too, from <Fig s="total" p={recPeak} m="received" /> in
      {" "}{quarterLabel(recPeak)} to <Fig s="total" p={L} m="received" />, but not as fast as decisions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Chart
    spec={seriesSpec("total", ["received", "approved"])}
    title="Applications received and approved per quarter, all USCIS forms"
    subtitle={`USCIS service-wide total, ${quarterLabel(F)} to ${quarterLabel(L)}.`}
  />
  <Chart spec={seriesSpec("total", ["pending"], { area: true })} title="Cases pending at the end of each quarter, all USCIS forms" />

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Citizenship: {natPrevLow === "FY2020Q3" && !natLow ? "fewer approvals than during the pandemic shutdown" : "approvals at a low"}</h2>
    <p>
      USCIS approved <Fig s="n-400" p={L} m="approved" /> naturalization applications (Form N-400) in
      {" "}{quarterLabel(L)}, {natLow ? `the fewest since ${quarterLabel(natLow)}` : `the fewest in any quarter since ${quarterLabel(F)}`}.
      The previous low was <Fig s="n-400" p={natPrevLow} m="approved" /> in {quarterLabel(natPrevLow)}
      {natPrevLow === "FY2020Q3" ? ", when USCIS offices were closed to the public for COVID-19" : ""}. A year earlier, in {quarterLabel(natYearAgo)}, it approved
      {" "}<Fig s="n-400" p={natYearAgo} m="approved" />. Pending applications rose to
      {" "}<Fig s="n-400" p={L} m="pending" />, and the median decided case took
      {" "}<Fig s="n-400" p={L} m="median_processing_months" /> months.
    </p>
  </section>
  <Chart spec={seriesSpec("n-400", ["received", "approved"])} title="Naturalization (N-400): received and approved per quarter" subtitle="Excludes military naturalizations, reported separately." />

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Asylum: approvals near zero</h2>
    <p>
      For affirmative asylum, claims filed with USCIS rather than in immigration court, the agency approved
      {" "}<Fig s="i-589" p={asyLowest} m="approved" /> applications in {quarterLabel(asyLowest)}, the fewest of any
      quarter since {quarterLabel(F)}. New filings fell from <Fig s="i-589" p={asyRecPeak} m="received" /> in
      {" "}{quarterLabel(asyRecPeak)} to <Fig s="i-589" p={L} m="received" /> in {quarterLabel(L)}
      {asyRecLow ? `, the fewest since ${quarterLabel(asyRecLow)}` : ""}. The backlog barely moved:
      {" "}<Fig s="i-589" p={L} m="pending" /> cases at the end of {quarterLabel(L)}, against
      {" "}<Fig s="i-589" p={F} m="pending" /> in {quarterLabel(F)}.
    </p>
  </section>
  <Chart spec={seriesSpec("i-589", ["pending"], { area: true })} title="Affirmative asylum (I-589): applications pending" />

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Families: a {otherWaitYears.toFixed(1)}-year median wait, before the visa line</h2>
    <p>
      Since {quarterLabel("FY2025Q1")} USCIS reports relative petitions in two rows. For spouses, parents and minor
      children of citizens, the median decided case in {quarterLabel(L)} took
      {" "}<Fig s="i-130-immediate-relative" p={L} m="median_processing_months" /> months. For every other relative,
      such as siblings and adult children, it took <Fig s="i-130-other-relative" p={L} m="median_processing_months" /> months,
      with <Fig s="i-130-other-relative" p={L} m="pending" /> petitions waiting. Approval only gets
      them into a second line, for a visa number: see <a href="/visa-queue/">the visa queue</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What the spreadsheets get wrong</h2>
    <p>
      Rebuilding the series exposed {errorCount} problems in the source files that a reader of any single
      spreadsheet would miss. The FY2024Q3 report repeats the previous quarter's median processing times, to seven or
      more significant digits, for {repeated} forms. Two snapshots of the family visa queue carry the wrong date in
      their titles. Several older files print numbers with no label at all. We kept every printed value and flagged it
      rather than "fixing" it. <a href="/source-errors/">Read the full list.</a>
    </p>

    <h2>What this does not tell you</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Why.</strong> The reports count cases. They don't explain policy, staffing or processing changes, and
        we don't attribute the decline to any of them. <a href="/methodology/#questions">Our open questions for USCIS</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Exact comparability across every year.</strong> USCIS has split, merged and renamed rows, and its
        total line has excluded some work in some years (its FY2021Q4 footnote: immigrant visas and EOIR adjustments
        are "not included in the Total - All Forms line"). Later reports also restate earlier quarters; we use the
        latest printing and keep every earlier one in the <a href="/data/v1/revisions.csv">revisions file</a>. Each
        series page lists its breaks.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your case.</strong> A median is the middle decided case, not a promise. Check{" "}
        <a href="https://egov.uscis.gov/processing-times/">USCIS's official processing times</a> for your field office.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="callout">
      <p><strong>Check our work.</strong> Click any underlined number to open the archived government file it came from.
      Hover to see the exact cell. The <a href="/data/">full dataset</a> is free to download, with all {nSources}{" "}
      source files, their SHA-256 hashes, and the code that parses them.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
